description.narrative:
UNESCO will strengthen Media and Information Literacy (MIL) across education, youth and media sectors through integrated policy support, curriculum development, institutional capacity-building and multistakeholder engagement. The project will support Member States and partner institutions in embedding MIL into education systems, public policies and professional practices, while promoting critical thinking, ethical engagement with information and inclusive participation in digital and media environments.
The project will focus on five mutually reinforcing areas:
1.	Strengthening national or regional MIL policies and governance frameworks to support coherent and sustainable approaches to MIL;
2.	Advancing MIL curricula and teacher training through updated educational resources and institutional capacity-building;
3.	Empowering youth to actively promote critical thinking; 
4.	Strengthening MIL in media ecosystems through partnerships with journalists, and media organizations.
5.	Supporting parents and families in strengthening critical thinking and safe digital engagement through digital parenting resources, guidance and community-based MIL initiatives;
6.	Advancing global dialogue, networking and knowledge sharing
Through these efforts, UNESCO will contribute to strengthening information integrity, resilience to misinformation and hate speech, and inclusive participation in digital and media environments.
